  body: "# Benefit entitlement in the captured custody guidance\n\nEntitlement and payability are distinct
    in the captured guidance, but entitlement can end under benefit-specific conditions. DMG 24185–24186,
    24212, 41823 and 54214 show why a payment-only statement cannot be generalised across JSA, IS and
    ESA. A nil Pension Credit award must be described using its own credit/award wording, not inferred
    from 12003.\n\n## Scope and limitations\n\nFrozen DMG research: listed legacy JSA(Cont), JSA(IB),
    IS, SPC and ESA(Cont)/ESA(IR) imprisonment guidance captured on 15 September 2026. This is an explanation
    of the captured text, not a determination of contemporary individual eligibility.\n\nIndependent experimental
    research, not an official DWP document, benefits advice, a calculation or an individual entitlement
    decision. All authored meanings and dependencies require specialist review.\n\nThe broad labels JSA
    and ESA do not establish a claimant’s regime. This profile explains the listed DMG legacy regimes;
    New Style JSA/ESA, UC and PIP are routed to ADM by 12016. Those ADM bodies are not acquired. Ask for
    regime/date and fresh authoritative checks before applying guidance to a person.\n\nThe payability
    statement at 12003 is scoped by the list in 12002. It cannot replace benefit-specific rules or establish
    that entitlement always survives imprisonment.\n\nMachine-extracted whole pages retain neighbouring
    text, partial unrelated paragraphs, footnotes, historical examples and possible reading-order errors.
    Use the stated locators; page presence is not full legal interpretation or PDF visual review.\n\n\
    Capture date is not publication, revision or commencement. Old amendment footers and example dates
    remain literal source text. The currently linked catalogue is not current-law assurance; legislation
    and case law have not been consolidated or reconciled.\n\nThe frozen PDFs still refer to Memo 07/20.
    Official catalogue history says it was removed because the regulations ceased to have effect from
    31 August 2021. The memo body is absent; do not revive that temporary exception.\n\n12016’s ADM M1
    reference conflicts with the frozen catalogue title marking M1 spare. S1/U6 are identified routes,
    not acquired evidence. Internal Chapter 41 references to 53112 and 53071 and the printed Chapter 53
    number 531261 remain unresolved version/typographic observations.\n\nPrisoner definitions differ by
    benefit: do not transfer the general criminal/civil distinction indiscriminately. Remand, bail hostel,
    sentence, release, hospital legislation, fine default, overseas detention, time limits and partner
    circumstances require the relevant branch. Housing-cost passages do not establish a current housing
    award."
